\begin{definition}[Total causal effect]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     \end{definition}
The fairness criterion defined on total causal effect claims that the prediction $\hat{Y}$ is fair with respect to the sensitive attribute $\mathbf{A}$ if $P(\hat{Y}=\hat{y}|do(\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{a}))=P(\hat{Y}=\hat{y}|do(\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{a'}))$ holds for all possible values of $\hat{y}$ and any value that $\mathbf{A}$ can take.

\citep{pearl2009causality}
